ts. It specifically targets older adults, providing a means to understand their nutritional needs and appetite levels effectively.", "RESIDENCIAS:Residences are facilities where elderly individuals live and where nutritional assessments are important for their care.", "PERSONAS MAYORES:\"PERSONAS MAYORES\" se refiere a un grupo poblacional que incluye a los adultos mayores, quienes pueden experimentar déficits significativos de zinc y cobre. Este grupo demográfico presenta necesidades específicas en cuanto a proteínas y otros nutrientes, lo que se discute en el contexto de la salud y la nutrición. Además, se considera que los adultos mayores están en un alto riesgo de desarrollar deficiencias de micronutrientes, especialmente de calcio, ácido fólico, vitamina A y vitamina D. Debido a sus diversas características y necesidades nutricionales, es fundamental implementar estrategias dietéticas personalizadas que promuevan un envejecimiento saludable.", "FPM:The Handgrip Strength Measurement is used to assess muscle strength in frail patients.", "BIVA:Bioimpedance Vector Analysis is a method that standardizes results from bioimpedance measurements.", "ALTA HOSPITALARIA:ALTA HOSPITALARIA refers to the discharge of a patient from the hospital after they have received treatment. This process, known as hospital discharge, involves releasing the patient from the hospital's care. A critical aspect of this transition is ensuring that the patient receives appropriate nutritional care, which is essential for their recovery following hospitalization.", "ÁLVAREZ-HERNÁNDEZ J:Álvarez-Hernández J is a researcher who focuses on malnutrition and its management within hospital settings. He has conducted studies examining the prevalence and costs associated with malnutrition in hospitalized patients, contributing valuable insights to the field. His work emphasizes the importance of addressing malnutrition to improve patient outcomes in healthcare environments.", "DENT E:A researcher who has conducted systematic reviews on nutritional screening tools for older adults.", "CRUZ-JENTOFT AJ:Cruz-Jentoft AJ is a prominent researcher associated with the European Working Group on Sarcopenia in Older People. He has made significant contributions to the consensus on sarcopenia, a condition characterized by the loss of muscle mass and strength in older adults. His research focuses on the implications of sarcopenia for this demographic, highlighting the importance of understanding and addressing this condition to improve the health and quality of life for older individuals.", "CLASIFICACIÓN INTERNACIONAL DE ENFERMEDADES:The Clasificación Internacional de Enfermedades (CIE), known in English as the International Classification of Diseases (ICD), is an international instrument developed by the World Health Organization (WHO) to identify health trends and statistics worldwide. This system is utilized for coding and classifying diseases and health conditions, providing a standardized framework for health data collection and analysis across different countries and healthcare systems.", "GUERRA RS:A researcher involved in studies related to malnutrition and its impact on health outcomes.", "NUTRITION 2012:Nutrition 2012 is a publication that discusses various aspects of nutrition, including hospital malnutrition."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}